{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"A routine fix round leaves a false review request that can prompt duplicate review work while changes are in progress."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"After an external merge, the persistent false blocker can send an agent to investigate work that is already complete."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A confirmed merge can be reported as unknown, prompting needless investigation and obscuring the run's actual state."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A new commit invalidates an approval without restoring the review request, so a needed review can be missed."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A historical failed round masks a subsequent valid approval and can prevent an agent from proceeding to landing."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"An answered question remains in the digest until a clearing event, causing repeated misleading prompts while the run continues."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"An empty filter now causes the list request to fail, although no known client sends that input."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"MCP approvals are persistently misattributed as human in the audit display, but the reviewer label affects no authorization decision."},{"id":"C9","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Status directs an agent to resolve an old blocker and retry landing even though the closed PR makes that request fail."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resolved or cancelled run remains listed for review, potentially causing an agent to spend effort on abandoned work."},{"id":"C11","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Following the Codex skill can omit unread items already acknowledged by Claude, causing a session to miss work needing attention."}]}